{# ---------- Timeline ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Plan ahead</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="timeline-title">Timeline for planning</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">Global programs reward early planning. A typical path from first curiosity to coming home looks like this.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>12+ months out: attend an information session</h3>
        <p>Hear from faculty liaisons and returning students, learn which programs fit your degree plan and join the OGE listserv so you do not miss a deadline.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>9 months out: talk to a faculty liaison</h3>
        <p>Ask about specific agencies, language expectations and what a week on site looks like. For the Global Practicum, loop in your practicum advisor so the placement meets your degree requirements.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>6 months out: apply</h3>
        <p>Submit your application by the priority deadline listed on each program page. Global Practicum applications run in the fall for spring placements; PUC applications are rolling with a spring priority deadline.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>3 months out: pre-departure preparation</h3>
        <p>Complete Texas Global requirements, confirm your passport and any visa, arrange funding and housing and attend pre-departure sessions on logistics and cultural orientation.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Go</h3>
        <p>Learn from practitioners and communities on their own ground, with your faculty liaison, the Global Practicum Seminar and OGE behind you.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Return and share your story</h3>
        <p>Present at a campus showcase, contribute a Global Story and help the next cohort decide to go.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Funding ---------- #}
<section class="section section--sand" aria-labelledby="funding-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Funding</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="funding-title">Funding your experience</h2>
        <p>Cost should not decide whether you go. Several sources can help, and OGE will walk through them with you.</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>School practicum funding programs.</strong> The School has grown its grant-funded practicum support programs substantially in recent years. Ask the Office of Practicum Education and OGE which programs apply to an international placement.</li>
          <li><strong>Texas Global scholarships.</strong> Texas Global offers scholarships and funding guidance for UT students studying abroad. Start at <a href="https://global.utexas.edu/abroad/funding">global.utexas.edu/abroad/funding</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>May Term tuition.</strong> Full-time undergraduate students pay no additional tuition for May Term courses, according to Texas Global; program fees and travel costs still apply.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">Costs and fees change each cycle. We do not publish amounts here; see the current application for each program and ask OGE about this year's funding.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split__media flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">Donors make this possible</p>
        <p>Immersive global education transforms students' lives for social work practice at home. Gifts to global engagement help send students abroad who could not otherwise go.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/give/">Support student travel</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- FAQ ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h3>Do I need to speak another language?</h3>
      <p>It depends on the placement. Fluent Spanish is required for clinical internships in Santiago, Chile and Oaxaca, Mexico. No language requirement is listed for Wellington, Cape Town, the UNHCR offices in Geneva and Budapest, the May Term courses or From Texas to the Troubles. Confirm expectations with the faculty liaison for the site you are considering.</p>

      <h3>Who is eligible?</h3>
      <p>The Global Practicum is for MSSW students completing their final advanced Clinical or APP practicum. Projects with Underserved Communities is for undergraduate social work and engineering students. May Term courses are open to undergraduate and graduate students (the Washington, D.C. course is explicitly open to both). From Texas to the Troubles welcomes students, faculty and staff. Each program page lists its current requirements.</p>

      <h3>Can I do a global practicum in my first year?</h3>
      <p>No. The Global Practicum is your final practicum, taken as an advanced Clinical or APP placement in the spring. First-year students should attend an information session, talk with a faculty liaison and plan so that their final practicum can be abroad.</p>

      <h3>How are safety and support handled?</h3>
      <p>OGE coordinates every placement with the Office of Practicum Education and Texas Global, the University's international office. Each practicum site has a designated faculty liaison, international interns meet in the Global Practicum Seminar, and pre-departure preparation covers expectations and logistics before you leave. If circumstances change on the ground, your liaison and OGE are your first calls.</p>

      <h3>Do I need a passport?</h3>
      <p>Yes, for every international program. Apply for or renew your passport as soon as you start planning; processing can take months. Visa requirements vary by country and program, and Texas Global will advise you on what your destination requires.</p>

      <h3>How do international students participate?</h3>
      <p>International students at the School are welcome in every program. Because travel can affect your visa status, talk with Texas Global's International Student &amp; Scholar Services (<a href="https://global.utexas.edu/isss">global.utexas.edu/isss</a>) before you apply, and see our <a href="/resources/international-students/">international student resources</a>.</p>

      <h3>What does it cost?</h3>
      <p>Costs differ by program and change each cycle, so we do not publish amounts on this page. The current application for each program lists fees, and the funding options above can offset them. Full-time undergraduates pay no additional tuition for May Term courses.</p>

      <h3>Who do I contact with questions about a specific site?</h3>
      <p>Reach out to the faculty liaison associated with that program: Anita Guajardo (Santiago and Oaxaca), Starla Simmons (Wellington), Tammy Linseisen (Cape Town) or Assistant Dean Stacey Jordan (UNHCR). For anything else, <a href="/connect/">contact OGE</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

